  "note": "Re-judged 2026-11-20 by an independent agent after df3221e7b8, 40cf3cfaec and a29420771d changed applyConfig and releaseSPD; no tagged unit changed. Parent quote, RFC 4301 Section 4.4.1: \"Every SPD SHOULD have a nominal, final entry that matches anything that is otherwise unmatched, and discards it.\" Tested: \"a nominal, final entry that matches anything that is otherwise unmatched, and discards it\". Gap: \"Every SPD\". Boundary producer: internal/component/ike/dataplane/vpp_policy.go::vppPolicyInterface. Producer changes read: the ICMP error return entries that ranked above the catch-all are gone from applyConfig and releaseSPD (the kernel maps forwarded ICMP errors), and the start-time warnForwardBypassAtStart only logs; installUnmatched still goes first on the first apply and removeUnmatched last on release. The tagged units still replay every Ze write and require the catch-all beneath it, discard an unmatched clear packet in the kernel at if_id 0 and on a bound XFRM interface, and fail the apply on a refused interface catch-all. Gap unchanged: no final entry on VPP SPDs or beneath the OSPF protocol 89 entries. Scoped evidence only; zero whole-requirement credit.",
